From: LilSmokeOS <local@lilsmoke.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] cap XZ decoder memory on the 128 MiB single CPU M8

The caller caps filesystem block size. The XZ stream header can still
request a much larger dictionary, so bound liblzma independently.

--- a/lib/sqfs/comp/xz.c
+++ b/lib/sqfs/comp/xz.c
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@
 static sqfs_s32 xz_uncomp_block(sqfs_compressor_t *base, const sqfs_u8 *in,
 			      sqfs_u32 size, sqfs_u8 *out, sqfs_u32 outsize)
 {
-	sqfs_u64 memlimit = 65 * 1024 * 1024;
+	sqfs_u64 memlimit = 8 * 1024 * 1024;
 	size_t dest_pos = 0;
 	size_t src_pos = 0;
 	lzma_ret ret;
